# Godot Visual Client / UI Boundary

This boundary governs the **Godot visual client/UI layer** (`godot_project/client/`). It is **non-authoritative**. The authoritative rules live in the **GDScript simulation core** (`godot_project/sim/`), governed by `03-godot-sim-authority.mdc`.

> The simulation core is authoritative even though it is also GDScript. "Godot is authoritative" is never correct — only the simulation core is.

## The UI client MAY

- Load snapshots from the simulation core and render 2D layers
- Submit player commands to the simulation core (never execute rules locally)
- Display diagnostics, replay timelines, and debug overlays
- Handle touch input, camera, and UI chrome
- Use floats for presentation-only animation (never fed back into authoritative state)

## The UI client MUST NOT

- Implement authoritative gameplay rules in scene/UI logic
- Maintain a parallel game state that diverges from simulation-core snapshots
- Generate gameplay randomness
- Hard-code economy chains, combat formulas, or production logic
- Mutate authoritative state directly (always go through commands)

## Adapter Contract

Follow `docs/architecture/03_godot_adapter_contract.md` for snapshot schema, command submission format, and layer rendering.

When in doubt: if it changes game state, it belongs in the simulation core (`sim/`), not the UI client (`client/`).
